var GR=[["Alchemist's Ice",50,1,"Alchemical","A blue-white flask, cool to the touch, holding a volatile liquid that turns to ice in air. Poured on a surface, it makes a 5-foot patch of ice that works as regular ice for movement. You can throw it like a flask of Alchemist's Fire. On a hit it deals 1d8 Cold damage, and the target makes a DC 10 Dexterity saving throw or has its Speed reduced to 0 until the start of your next turn."],["Hypodermic Arrow",25,0.05,"Ammunition","An arrow with a syringe for a head. When it hits a creature it deals 1d4 Piercing damage plus the effect of whatever liquid the syringe injects, such as poison, acid, drugs, or potions. It always breaks on impact, hit or miss. It is sold empty, though ones found in hoards may be filled. Filling the syringe takes an action and can be done hours or days ahead."],["Swarm Repellent",40,1,"Alchemical","A slimy yellow paste smeared on exposed skin. A swarm of ants, beetles, biting flies, wasps, or similar insects that enters your space must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution saving throw or be unable to attack you. A repelled swarm repeats the save at the start of its next turn, and most swarms look for easier prey. One jar protects two Medium or four Small creatures. Applying it takes 1 minute. It works for 1 hour or until you are immersed in water."],["Tooth Capsule",100,0,"Alchemical","A false tooth, or a cap over a real one, holding one dose of a potion in pill form. The pill cannot be swapped out. To use it, bite down as a Bonus Action and make a DC 10 Strength check. On a success, the capsule breaks and you can swallow, hold, or spit out the pill. Spotting a tooth capsule in another creature's mouth needs a DC 15 Intelligence (Investigation) or Wisdom (Medicine) check, and the creature must be Restrained, Unconscious, Paralyzed, or cooperative. Spies and fanatics often load them with poison. The price is 100 gp plus the cost of the loaded potion, and some places outlaw harmful contents, which raises black market prices."]];
